diff --git a/docs/amd64-cross-args.gn b/docs/amd64-cross-args.gn
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..92466a4615
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/amd64-cross-args.gn
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Release build args for Antimony amd64, cross-compiled on the arm64
+# HIGH-MEM box (patch 0022, series base 507c6ee3e2).
+# Copy to out/amd64-release/args.gn before running gn gen.
+#
+# is_official_build=true enables optimization + thin LTO + CFI and the
+# installer strips the packaged binary: the amd64 deb came out at 126.5 MB
+# vs 581 MB for the unofficial build (antimony-v153.0.8010.36).
+# chrome_pgo_phase=0 because no PGO profile is provisioned for the
+# custom-toolchain cross setup.
+#
+# See docs/amd64-cross-build.md for the one-time cross-environment setup
+# (amd64 sysroot, x64 rust std, CFI sanitizer share files, env vars).
+
+is_debug = false
+is_component_build = false
+is_official_build = true
+chrome_pgo_phase = 0
+symbol_level = 0
+blink_symbol_level = 0
+v8_symbol_level = 0
+treat_warnings_as_errors = false
+target_cpu = "x64"
+clang_base_path = "/home/ubuntu/chromium-build/src/third_party/rust-toolchain-intermediate/llvm-host-install"
+clang_use_chrome_plugins = false
+rust_bindgen_root = "//third_party/rust-toolchain-intermediate/llvm-host-install"
diff --git a/docs/amd64-cross-build.md b/docs/amd64-cross-build.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..6ba8102656
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/amd64-cross-build.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# Antimony amd64 cross-build (arm64 host -> x64 target)
+
+Verified end-to-end on the HIGH-MEM box (2026-10-06/07): full official
+chrome cross build plus chrome/installer/linux:stable_deb produced
+antimony-stable_153.0.8010.36-1_amd64.deb at 126.5 MB (stripped binary,
+thin LTO + CFI) vs 581 MB for the unstripped unofficial build.
+
+## One-time cross-environment setup
+
+1. amd64 sysroot (only the arm64 one is staged by default):
+   python3 build/linux/sysroot_scripts/install-sysroot.py --arch=amd64
+
+2. Toolchain def (patch 0022): adds clang_arm64_v8_x64 to
+   build/toolchain/linux/BUILD.gn so the v8 snapshot/generator host tools
+   get an arm64-host toolchain when target_cpu="x64". Without it gn gen
+   fails with "Unresolved dependencies" naming that toolchain (macOS
+   defines the equivalent; Linux never did).
+
+3. x64 rust std: the locally built toolchain stages only
+   aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu std. Build x64 std WITH THE INSTALLED rustc
+   so crate metadata matches - the x.py/bootstrap route rebuilds rustc
+   with an unstamped version string and rustc then rejects its own std
+   (E0514 incompatible version):
+   - ln -sfn $SRC/third_party/rust-src third_party/rust-toolchain/lib/rustlib/src/rust
+   - scratch cargo project; RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 cargo build --release
+     --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -Z build-std=std with
+     CARGO_TARGET_X86_64_UNKNOWN_LINUX_GNU_LINKER=/tmp/x64-clang-linker.sh
+     and CFLAGS_x86_64_unknown_linux_gnu="--sysroot=<amd64 sysroot>"
+   - stage the resulting *.rlib into third_party/rust-toolchain/lib/
+     rustlib/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/
+
+4. Wrapper linker /tmp/x64-clang-linker.sh (tmpfs - recreate per boot):
+   #!/bin/sh
+   exec <toolchain>/bin/clang --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu \
+     --sysroot=<amd64 sysroot> -fuse-ld=lld "$@"
+   (-fuse-ld=lld is required: without it clang's linker probe picks the
+   host aarch64 bfd, which rejects x86_64 emulation.)
+
+5. TypeScript devtools steps: third_party/typescript ships an amd64-only
+   tsc 3pp bundle; the aarch64 tsc exists at linux-arm64/src/lib/tsc and
+   typescript.py selects it via platform.machine(), but official-config
+   devtools actions invoke the linux-amd64 path directly. Tree-local
+   (NOT committed; recreate per checkout):
+   ln -s ../../../linux-arm64/src/lib/tsc \
+     third_party/typescript/linux-amd64/src/lib/tsc
+
+6. qemu-user fallback: apt install qemu-user qemu-user-binfmt - binfmt
+   registers x86_64 so any other amd64-only host tool still runs on the
+   arm64 host (qemu-user-static no longer exists on Ubuntu 26.04).
+
+7. CFI sanitizer share files: is_official_build enables CFI
+   (-fsanitize=cfi-vcall/icall + -fwhole-program-vtables); the locally
+   built toolchain's clang resource dir lacks the default ignorelists
+   (clang++: error: missing sanitizer ignorelist). Download the official
+   chromium clang package at the tree's pinned revision
+   (tools/clang/scripts/update.py PACKAGE_VERSION =
+   llvmorg-24-init-3796-g20e97c4b-2) and copy
+   lib/clang/24/share/{cfi,asan,msan}_ignorelist.txt into
+   <toolchain>/lib/clang/24/share/.
+
+8. Env vars (the bridge runs as root with no HOME):
+   HOME=/tmp GOCACHE=/tmp/go-cache GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/tmp/gitconfig-build
+   with /tmp/gitconfig-build containing [safe] directory = *
+   (dawn's generate-sources needs GOCACHE; angle's commit_id and any git
+   call need safe.directory; both fail without them).
+
+## Build
+
+    cp docs/amd64-cross-args.gn out/amd64-release/args.gn
+    <gn-cipd>/gn gen out/amd64-release
+    ninja -C out/amd64-release chrome
+    ninja -C out/amd64-release chrome/installer/linux:stable_deb
+
+Deb verification: dpkg-deb -I shows antimony-stable / amd64; extract and
+check the inner /opt/antimony/chrome is x86-64 AND stripped
+(readelf -S | grep -c symtab == 0).
+
+## Pitfalls (all paid for once)
+
+- Abrupt halts and ninja kills TRUNCATE in-flight outputs while leaving
+  them "fresh" by mtime: after any halt, gn gen, then
+  find out/<dir> -type f \( -name '*.rlib' -o -name '*.rmeta' \
+    -o -name '*.o' -o -name '*.a' -o -name '*.so' \) -size 0 -delete
+  and check devtools gen outputs for tiny truncations (a 35-byte
+  marked.js / 0-byte marked.d.ts surfaced as TS2306 "is not a module"
+  several thousand steps later).
+- First gn gen without the toolchain def fails listing
+  clang_arm64_v8_x64 as unresolved - that IS the patch's job.
+- The x64 rust std MUST be compiled by the installed toolchain rustc;
+  a bootstrap-rebuilt rustc's std is rejected (E0514).
